# Part 6 --- Capstone and professional readiness

## Phase 15: Build two substantial end-to-end projects

**Duration:** 4--6 weeks

Build projects that demonstrate both ML understanding and software
engineering ability.

### Capstone A: Business prediction system

Possible problem: - Customer churn prediction. - Sales forecasting. -
Lead conversion prediction. - Demand forecasting.

Deliverables: - Problem statement and success metric. - Data-quality and
exploratory analysis. - Baseline. - Feature engineering. - Correct
validation strategy. - Model comparison. - Error analysis. - Model
interpretation. - API deployment. - Monitoring plan. - README with
reproducible steps.

### Capstone B: LLM application

Possible problem: - Document intelligence and RAG. - Knowledge-base
assistant. - Support-ticket classification and retrieval. - Tool-using
workflow assistant.

Deliverables: - Data ingestion. - Chunking and indexing. - Retrieval and
reranking. - Answer generation. - Evaluation dataset. - Retrieval and
answer metrics. - Hallucination and failure analysis. - Security and
privacy considerations. - Deployment and monitoring.

### Portfolio standards

For each project: - Keep code in a clean Git repository. - Explain the
problem and why ML is appropriate. - Include a simple baseline. -
Document data sources and limitations. - Prevent data leakage. - Explain
metric selection. - Include reproducible setup and run instructions. -
Show examples of failure, not only successful predictions. - State what
you would improve next.

